1
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Adventure has a new name.

2
00:06:54,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Lady and the Tramp II: Scamp's Adventure is a family,
animation, romance film directed by Darrell Rooney.

3
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Lady and Tramp's mischievous pup, Scamp, gets fed up with rules and restrictions
imposed on him by life in a family, and longs for a wild and free lifestyle.

4
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:54,000
He runs away from home and into the streets where he joins a pack of stray dogs known as the "Junkyard Dogs."
Buster, the pack's leader, takes an instant disliking to the "house-dog" and considers him a rival.

5
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Angel, a junkyard pup Scamp's age, longs for the safety and comfort of
life in a family and the two become instant companions.

6
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Will Scamp choose the wild and free life of a stray or
the unconditional love of his family?

7
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:15,000
Scamp (speaking) (voice), played by Scott Wolf.

8
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Angel (speaking) (voice), played by Alyssa Milano.

9
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:09,000
Buster (speaking) (voice), played by Chazz Palminteri.

10
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Tramp / Jock / Trusty / Dogcatcher (voice), played by Jeff Bennett.

11
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:03,000
Lady (voice), played by Jodi Benson.

12
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Mooch (voice), played by Bill Fagerbakke.

13
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:57,000
Lady and the Tramp II: Scamp's Adventure is a 2001 American animated direct-to-video musical romantic comedy film produced by
Walt Disney Television Animation, and the sequel to Disney's 1955 animated feature film Lady and the Tramp.

14
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:24,000
The film was directed by Darrell Rooney and Jeannine Roussel,
with a screenplay by Bill Motz and Bob Roth.

15
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:51,000
It stars Scott Wolf as Lady and Tramp's son Scamp,
who desires to become a wild dog.

16
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
In the film, Scamp runs away from his home and joins a gang of stray dogs called the
Junkyard Dogs, where he falls in love with one of the gang's members, Angel.

17
00:58:39,000 --> 00:58:45,000
Lady and the Tramp II: Scamp's Adventure was released on
February 27, 2001, to mixed reviews from critics.

18
01:02:06,000 --> 01:02:12,000
The film explores themes of cartoon, sequel,
initiation, cartoon dog, dogcatcher.

19
01:05:33,000 --> 01:05:39,000
The tone is emotional.
